      "reasons": [
        "The first sentence gives a broad general definition of psychosocial support as help to improve emotional and social wellbeing and reduce loneliness/negative feelings, but the packet only says the adolescents had risks of those problems and limited access to acceptable psychosocial support; it does not define the term that way.",
        "The second sentence adds an interpretation about what the term refers to in this context, but the packet only supports a culturally grounded school-based psychosocial support programme and notes that conventional school counselling often depends on self-referral and verbal disclosure; it does not explicitly define psychosocial support as not relying only on students openly identifying themselves as needing help."
